<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antigua and Barbuda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antigua and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbuda">Barbuda</a> is an archipelagic country in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> made up of Antigua, Barbuda and dozens of smaller islands. Hunter-gatherers settled the islands long before European contact, probably arriving by canoe from Central and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>. After a failed Spanish attempt in 1520, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-warner">Edward Warner</a> founded the first successful British colony in 1632, and Barbuda was long controlled by the Codrington family. Autonomy grew slowly after emancipation in 1834, and the first democratic elections were held in 1951. Antigua and Barbuda gained full independence on 1 November 1981 and remains a Commonwealth realm.</p></div>
